  "response_text": "The __io_putchar function is used to send a single character out through the UART, and it is required in order for the printf function to work on the microcontroller. Although printf is part of the standard C library, it doesn\u2019t know how to send characters to hardware by default. On embedded systems, we must manually connect printf to UART2.\\n",
